title: 'tests can synthesize and play real audio: B188 gates ducking but not TTS playback or provider spend'
updated_at: "2026-10-26T00:20:39Z"
---
Follow-on from B188. That task gated the MUTATING media-control commands (volume duck, MPRIS pause, capture mute). It did NOT gate the two other ways a test reaches the operator: making noise, and spending money.

Concrete incident 2026-08-23: the B186 implementation agent ran `hark tts --text "Ready?"` without --listen in a verification step where it had stubbed speak_and_listen but not run_tts. Result: one real provider synthesis (billable) plus one real playback on the shared desktop, and a cache write to assets/tts/eve/ready-95c05077.mp3. Self-reported, and the agent stubbed run_tts for all later checks. This is a foreseeable mistake, not a careless one - the stub surface is not obvious.

Two seams:

1. PLAYBACK (noise on the operator desktop)
   - src/hark/audio/playback.py:1352-1354 spawns ffplay / paplay / aplay
   - src/hark/audio/playback.py:1338 sd.play(samples, sample_rate) + sd.wait()
   Note ffmpeg at :1300, :1395 and :1430 is CONVERSION, not playback - silent and harmless. Do not blanket-block ffmpeg or you break MP3 handling tests.

2. PROVIDER SPEND (real money, real network)
   - src/hark/speech.py:684 run_tts
   - the provider HTTP path under src/hark/providers/
   A test that reaches a live TTS/STT endpoint costs credit and is slow and flaky. There is no test-time network guard today; conftest only disables the GitHub update check (B088).

Recommended shape, mirroring B188 so there is one idiom rather than three:
- extend hark.audio.external_audio with is_audio_playback_argv() and have the conftest tripwire fail on ffplay/paplay/aplay
- add a conftest fixture that wraps sounddevice play so a test that reaches the real device fails loudly
- separately (larger, decide scope first): fail a test that opens an outbound HTTP connection to a provider unless it opts in, so accidental live synthesis is a red test rather than a line item. Live-dogfood tests like B183 must be able to opt in.

The playback half is cheap and test-only. The spend half needs a decision about how live-verify tasks opt in.

PARTIALLY DONE 2026-08-23 (f46a42a). The PLAYBACK half is landed: conftest tripwires fail any test that spawns ffplay/paplay/aplay or reaches sounddevice.play; external_audio.is_audio_playback_argv() classifies players; ffmpeg is explicitly excluded (it converts, silently) and a test pins that so nobody folds it into the player set later. Test-only, no production behaviour change. Suite 6230 passed / 0 failed.

STILL OPEN - the PROVIDER SPEND half. A test can still reach a live TTS/STT endpoint and bill it: src/hark/speech.py:684 run_tts and the provider HTTP path under src/hark/providers/. There is no test-time network guard; conftest only disables the GitHub update check (B088).

Blocked on a decision, not on effort: live-dogfood tasks (see B183, live-verify Custom STT + Custom TTS against a real gateway) MUST be able to reach the network, so any guard needs an opt-in that those tasks use deliberately. Options, in rough order of preference:
1. Block outbound connections at the socket layer under pytest, opt in via a marker plus an env var. Strongest and catches paths nobody predicted; needs care not to break localhost fixtures (dashboard server tests bind sockets).
2. Guard only the provider layer (a check inside the HTTP helper in src/hark/providers/). Narrower, cannot catch a new code path that builds its own request, but zero risk to socket-using tests.
3. Do nothing and rely on stubbing discipline. Rejected in spirit by this whole task - the B186 incident is exactly what discipline alone gives you.

Recommend 2 first (cheap, no collateral), then 1 if accidental live calls recur. Do not start either without confirming how B183-style live verification opts in.

ARM-CUE PLAYBACK PATH, found by the B187/B177 agent 2026-08-23 while adding an answer-window nudge test. It saw sounddevice deprecation warnings, which meant the test was reaching the real audio stack.

Mechanism: run_listen reaches playback through the ARM-CUE path, not only through run_tts. So a test author who stubs run_tts alone still hits the device. The B190 tripwires DO catch it (the cue goes out through ffplay/paplay/aplay or sounddevice.play), which is the whole point - but the catch is what makes the tripwire worth having, since stubbing discipline alone would not have found it.

Correct fix pattern, for anyone hitting a B190 assertion: mirror the stubs in tests/test_empty_stt.py::_patch_listen_infra - play_record_start, play_record_stop, duck_media, MicLease, configure_cues_from_config. Better still, stub at the PROVIDER seam (hark.speech.resolve_tts) rather than at run_tts: that exercises the whole ladder with no network and no device, which is what you want if the code under test involves the B177 fallback.

Do NOT reach for @pytest.mark.allow_media_control to silence a B190 assertion. The marker exists for a test that must genuinely drive real argvs; using it to quiet an over-broad stub surface reintroduces exactly the incident this task was filed for.

Decision 2026-10-26: resolve design blocker with explicit dual opt-in for live-provider verification: pytest marker allow_provider_network plus HARK_TEST_PROVIDER_NETWORK=1; normal pytest blocks external provider HTTP while loopback fixtures and mocked transports remain allowed, and policy must carry into spawned Python children. B183-style dogfood uses explicit opt-in; no blanket media-control exemption. Test-only guard implementation separate from production provider fallback; conftest provider region separate from signal fixture region. Playback protection must include new RawOutputStream boundary.

Final verification 2026-10-26: reviewed fix merged to master. Integrated x-tall CPython3.13.11 suite: 6525 passed, 104 skipped, 0 failed in151.61s. Independent review and parent review passed. Full receipt /tmp/hark-b135-full-final.log; per-task evidence and design above. Normal pytest blocks external socket/provider IO in process and guarded Python children; loopback/mocks allowed. Live verification requires marker plus explicit environment opt-in. RawOutputStream tripwire independent of media-control exemption. No live external calls used.